{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786428898,"nonce":"i+kDF/Y+LouSUUp0ZvtFxsuRTSc=","message":"Fixed. The webhook provider now honours the same server-level security.allow_insecure_tls gate as sources. With it false, a per-channel insecure_skip_verify is REFUSED at validation (422, code insecure_skip_verify_not_permitted, violation field config/insecure_skip_verify) rather than silently ignored, mirroring sources/api.checkTLSSkipVerify. The served JSON Schema is now conditional: with the gate off the property is pruned from the descriptor, so the settings form cannot offer a control the server would 422.\n\nOpen() deliberately does NOT reject a stored pre-gate config — it ignores the flag and delivers WITH verification, exactly as sources does. Rejecting at Open would turn hardening into silent non-delivery for existing channels. Tests cover both settings, including a real httptest.NewTLSServer so the socket is asked what it did rather than the provider what it intended.\n\nLeft open: SPEC §L.5.2 still prints the webhook schema including insecure_skip_verify and lists only two server-side rules. Now stale on both counts; wants an amendment + ADR.","files":null}]}